245444.missionDescription:
Expand CPA is a French-American accounting and advisory firm specializing in supporting companies and individuals with cross-border operations between France and the United States.

As part of the continued development of our U.S. operations, we are looking for a V.I.E to join our Miami-based team and contribute to the growth and structuring of our activities in the United States.

Working closely with our U.S. Branch Manager and our teams in France and the United States, the V.I.E will participate in several areas:

* Support the development of our U.S. activities and the expansion of our French-American client base;
* Participate in the onboarding and coordination of French companies establishing or developing operations in the United States;
* Assist with the implementation and improvement of internal processes between our French and U.S. teams;
* Contribute to client relationship management and coordination of cross-border engagements;
* Participate in the development of reporting tools and operational procedures for the U.S. office;
* Support business development initiatives and partnerships in the U.S. market;
* Participate in the analysis and improvement of workflows between the Paris and Miami offices;
* Develop practical knowledge of the U.S. business, accounting and tax environment through close collaboration with experienced professionals.

This V.I.E assignment is designed to provide a strong learning and professional development experience in an international, entrepreneurial and multicultural environment. It will offer the V.I.E a unique opportunity to develop an in-depth understanding of cross-border business between France and the United States while acquiring practical skills in business development, international project management, client support and operational organization.

The V.I.E will receive ongoing guidance and mentoring from experienced professionals based in both France and the United States. This close supervision will allow the V.I.E to progressively develop a strong understanding of the U.S. business, accounting and tax environment while actively contributing to the growth and development of our Miami office.

The mission will therefore provide significant exposure to an international and entrepreneurial environment and will allow the V.I.E to develop strong skills in cross-border operations, business development and the U.S. professional services market.

The V.I.E will be based in Miami, Florida, and will work under the supervision of the U.S. Branch Manager, in close coordination with the Paris team.

